{"repo": "celery/celery", "pull_number": 11021, "instance_id": "celery__celery-11021", "issue_numbers": ["11003"], "base_commit": "e82fa93f539bc2eb0237417382fad02f42452532", "patch": "diff --git a/README.rst b/README.rst\nindex 2089d6d8edc..4960e9a1fa3 100644\n--- a/README.rst\n+++ b/README.rst\n@@ -470,7 +470,7 @@ pip commands:\n     $ pip install https://github.com/celery/billiard/zipball/main#egg=billiard\n     $ pip install https://github.com/celery/py-amqp/zipball/main#egg=amqp\n     $ pip install https://github.com/celery/kombu/zipball/main#egg=kombu\n-    $ pip install https://github.com/celery/vine/zipball/main#egg=vine\n+    $ pip install https://github.com/celery/vine/zipball/master#egg=vine\n \n With git\n ~~~~~~~~\ndiff --git a/docs/includes/installation.txt b/docs/includes/installation.txt\nindex db80860ef63..263a0db8bde 100644\n--- a/docs/includes/installation.txt\n+++ b/docs/includes/installation.txt\n@@ -166,7 +166,7 @@ pip commands:\n     $ pip install https://github.com/celery/billiard/zipball/main#egg=billiard\n     $ pip install https://github.com/celery/py-amqp/zipball/main#egg=amqp\n     $ pip install https://github.com/celery/kombu/zipball/main#egg=kombu\n-    $ pip install https://github.com/celery/vine/zipball/main#egg=vine\n+    $ pip install https://github.com/celery/vine/zipball/master#egg=vine\n \n With git\n ~~~~~~~~\ndiff --git a/docs/userguide/tasks.rst b/docs/userguide/tasks.rst\nindex f16e7833888..2f42e490ae9 100644\n--- a/docs/userguide/tasks.rst\n+++ b/docs/userguide/tasks.rst\n@@ -2465,7 +2465,7 @@ To make API calls to `Akismet`_ I use the `akismet.py`_ library written by\n \n         return is_spam\n \n-.. _`Akismet`: http://akismet.com/faq/\n+.. _`Akismet`: https://akismet.com/\n .. _`akismet.py`: http://www.voidspace.org.uk/downloads/akismet.py\n .. _`Michael Foord`: http://www.voidspace.org.uk/\n .. _`exponential backoff`: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Exponential_backoff\n", "test_patch": "", "problem_statement": "Docs: dead links in tasks guide and installation instructions (Akismet, vine zipball)\nWhile checking the documentation for dead links, I found two on `main` that are not covered by the open PR #10934:\n\n1. `docs/userguide/tasks.rst` - the `Akismet` link target `http://akismet.com/faq/` returns 404 (the FAQ page was retired). `https://akismet.com/` works.\n2. `docs/includes/installation.txt` - the line `pip install https://github.com/celery/vine/zipball/main#egg=vine` fails: the vine repository's default branch is `master`, so `/zipball/main` returns 404 while `/zipball/master` downloads fine. The sibling lines (celery, billiard, py-amqp, kombu) are correct since those repos use `main`.\n\nBoth verified just now (2026-11-02). Happy to open a small PR with these two one-line fixes if that is welcome.\n\nNote: this report was prepared with AI assistance and verified manually; per the anti-AI-spam policy I am asking here before submitting any PR.\n", "hints_text": "", "created_at": "2026-11-05T08:45:19Z"}
{"repo": "celery/celery", "pull_number": 11009, "instance_id": "celery__celery-11009", "issue_numbers": ["11008"], "base_commit": "1f435e5c718c8485143910d67b40eb164fd9f567", "patch": "diff --git a/celery/worker/request.py b/celery/worker/request.py\nindex d3afc52610f..237f7e57c98 100644\n--- a/celery/worker/request.py\n+++ b/celery/worker/request.py\n@@ -819,9 +819,12 @@ def _retry_worker_lost(self, exc, exc_info):\n                   self.task_name, self.id, send_exc, exc_info=True)\n             return False\n \n-        task.backend.mark_as_retry(\n-            self.id, exc, exc_info.traceback, request=request,\n-        )\n+        # As Task.retry() does: an ignored result isn't stored, so the\n+        # retried run wouldn't replace this RETRY with its outcome.\n+        if self.store_errors:\n+            task.backend.mark_as_retry(\n+                self.id, exc, exc_info.traceback, request=request,\n+            )\n         if task.acks_late:\n             self.acknowledge()\n         self.send_event('task-retried',\n", "test_patch": "diff --git a/t/unit/worker/test_request.py b/t/unit/worker/test_request.py\nindex 6090249f646..b831bd05c09 100644\n--- a/t/unit/worker/test_request.py\n+++ b/t/unit/worker/test_request.py\n@@ -476,13 +476,14 @@ def test_on_failure_WorkerLostError_rejects_with_requeue(self):\n             req_logger, req.connection_errors, True)\n         req.task.backend.mark_as_failure.assert_not_called()\n \n-    def _worker_lost_request(self, retries=0):\n+    def _worker_lost_request(self, retries=0, **options):\n         try:\n             raise WorkerLostError()\n         except WorkerLostError:\n             einfo = ExceptionInfo(internal=True)\n \n-        req = self.get_request(self.add.s(2, 2).set(retries=retries))\n+        req = self.get_request(\n+            self.add.s(2, 2).set(retries=retries, **options))\n         req.task.acks_late = True\n         req.task.reject_on_worker_lost = True\n         req.task.retry_on_worker_lost = True\n@@ -577,6 +578,39 @@ def test_on_failure_WorkerLostError_retry_on_worker_lost_no_acks_late(self):\n         req.on_ack.assert_not_called()\n         req.task.backend.mark_as_failure.assert_not_called()\n \n+    @pytest.mark.parametrize('ignored_by', ['task', 'call'])\n+    def test_on_failure_WorkerLostError_retry_on_worker_lost_ignore_result(\n+            self, ignored_by):\n+        # Like Task.retry(), don't store RETRY for a result that is ignored:\n+        # the retried run won't store anything, so RETRY would stay for good.\n+        if ignored_by == 'task':\n+            self.add.ignore_result = True\n+            req, einfo = self._worker_lost_request()\n+        else:\n+            req, einfo = self._worker_lost_request(ignore_result=True)\n+\n+        with patch('celery.canvas.Signature.apply_async') as apply_async:\n+            req.on_failure(einfo)\n+\n+        apply_async.assert_called_once()\n+        req.on_ack.assert_called_once()\n+        req.on_reject.assert_not_called()\n+        req.task.backend.mark_as_retry.assert_not_called()\n+        req.task.backend.mark_as_failure.assert_not_called()\n+        assert any(\n+            c.args and c.args[0] == 'task-retried'\n+            for c in req.eventer.send.call_args_list\n+        )\n+\n+    def test_on_failure_WorkerLostError_retry_on_worker_lost_store_errors_even_if_ignored(self):\n+        req, einfo = self._worker_lost_request(ignore_result=True)\n+        req.task.store_errors_even_if_ignored = True\n+\n+        with patch('celery.canvas.Signature.apply_async'):\n+            req.on_failure(einfo)\n+\n+        req.task.backend.mark_as_retry.assert_called_once()\n+\n     def test_on_failure_WorkerLostError_redelivered_None(self):\n         try:\n             raise WorkerLostError()\n", "problem_statement": "task_retry_on_worker_lost stores RETRY for a task whose result is ignored, and it stays RETRY\n<!--\nPlease fill this template entirely and do not erase parts of it.\nWe reserve the right to close without a response\nbug reports which are incomplete.\n-->\n# Checklist\n<!--\nTo check an item on the list replace [ ] with [x].\n-->\n- [x] I have verified that the issue exists against the `main` branch of Celery.\n- [ ] This has already been asked to the [discussions forum](https://github.com/celery/celery/discussions) first.\n- [x] I have read the relevant section in the\n  [contribution guide](https://docs.celeryq.dev/en/main/contributing.html#other-bugs)\n  on reporting bugs.\n- [x] I have checked the [issues list](https://github.com/celery/celery/issues?q=is%3Aissue+label%3A%22Issue+Type%3A+Bug+Report%22+-label%3A%22Category%3A+Documentation%22)\n  for similar or identical bug reports.\n- [x] I have checked the [pull requests list](https://github.com/celery/celery/pulls?q=is%3Apr+label%3A%22PR+Type%3A+Bugfix%22+-label%3A%22Category%3A+Documentation%22)\n  for existing proposed fixes.\n- [x] I have checked the [commit log](https://github.com/celery/celery/commits/main)\n  to find out if the bug was already fixed in the main branch.\n- [x] I have included all related issues and possible duplicate issues\n  in this issue (If there are none, check this box anyway).\n- [ ] I have tried to reproduce the issue with [pytest-celery](https://docs.celeryq.dev/projects/pytest-celery/en/latest/userguide/celery-bug-report.html) and added the reproduction script below.\n\n## Mandatory Debugging Information\n\n- [x] I have included the output of ``celery -A proj report`` in the issue.\n    (if you are not able to do this, then at least specify the Celery\n     version affected).\n- [x] I have verified that the issue exists against the `main` branch of Celery.\n- [x] I have included the contents of ``pip freeze`` in the issue.\n- [x] I have included all the versions of all the external dependencies required\n  to reproduce this bug.\n\n## Optional Debugging Information\n<!--\nTry some of the below if you think they are relevant.\nIt will help us figure out the scope of the bug and how many users it affects.\n-->\n- [ ] I have tried reproducing the issue on more than one Python version\n  and/or implementation.\n- [ ] I have tried reproducing the issue on more than one message broker and/or\n  result backend.\n- [ ] I have tried reproducing the issue on more than one version of the message\n  broker and/or result backend.\n- [ ] I have tried reproducing the issue on more than one operating system.\n- [ ] I have tried reproducing the issue on more than one workers pool.\n- [x] I have tried reproducing the issue with autoscaling, retries,\n  ETA/Countdown & rate limits disabled.\n- [ ] I have tried reproducing the issue after downgrading\n  and/or upgrading Celery and its dependencies.\n\n## Related Issues and Possible Duplicates\n<!--\nPlease make sure to search and mention any related issues\nor possible duplicates to this issue as requested by the checklist above.\n\nThis may or may not include issues in other repositories that the Celery project\nmaintains or other repositories that are dependencies of Celery.\n\nIf you don't know how to mention issues, please refer to Github's documentation\non the subject: https://help.github.com/en/articles/autolinked-references-and-urls#issues-and-pull-requests\n-->\n\n#### Related Issues\n\n- #10843 added `task_retry_on_worker_lost` and `Request._retry_worker_lost()`. It's in 5.7.0rc1 and not in a final release yet.\n- This was mentioned in passing in a review comment on #10958 (the table's last row there), as a separate bug. I couldn't find an issue for it.\n\n#### Possible Duplicates\n\n- None\n\n## Environment & Settings\n<!-- Include the contents of celery --version below -->\n**Celery version**: 5.7.0rc1 (`main` at 98b7ba94a)\n<!-- Include the output of celery -A proj report below -->\n<details>\n<summary><b><code>celery report</code> Output:</b></summary>\n<p>\n\n```\nsoftware -> celery:5.7.0rc1 (collider) kombu:5.7.0 py:3.14.5\n            billiard:4.3.2 filesystem:N/A\nplatform -> system:Darwin arch:64bit, Mach-O\n            kernel version:25.4.0 imp:CPython\nloader   -> celery.loaders.app.AppLoader\nsettings -> transport:filesystem results:file:///tmp/repro/results\n\nbroker_url: 'filesystem://:********@localhost//'\nresult_backend: 'file:///tmp/repro/results'\ndeprecated_settings: None\nbroker_transport_options:\n    'data_folder_in': '/tmp/repro/q',\n    'data_folder_out': '/tmp/repro/q',\n    'processed_folder': '/tmp/repro/processed'}\ntask_retry_on_worker_lost: True\n```\n\n</p>\n</details>\n\n# Steps to Reproduce\n\n## Required Dependencies\n<!-- Please fill the required dependencies to reproduce this issue -->\n- **Minimal Python Version**: N/A or Unknown\n- **Minimal Celery Version**: 5.7.0rc1 (`task_retry_on_worker_lost` was added there)\n- **Minimal Kombu Version**: N/A or Unknown\n- **Minimal Broker Version**: N/A or Unknown\n- **Minimal Result Backend Version**: N/A or Unknown\n- **Minimal OS and/or Kernel Version**: N/A or Unknown\n- **Minimal Broker Client Version**: N/A or Unknown\n- **Minimal Result Backend Client Version**: N/A or Unknown\n\n### Python Packages\n<!-- Please fill the contents of pip freeze below -->\n<details>\n<summary><b><code>pip freeze</code> Output:</b></summary>\n<p>\n\nCelery itself was run from a checkout of `main` (98b7ba94a) through `PYTHONPATH`. The packages it needs:\n\n```\namqp==5.4.2\nbilliard==4.3.2\nclick==8.5.0\nclick-didyoumean==0.3.1\nclick-plugins==1.1.1.2\nclick-repl==0.4.1\nkombu==5.7.0\npython-dateutil==2.9.0.post0\ntzlocal==5.4.5\nvine==5.1.0\n```\n\n</p>\n</details>\n\n### Other Dependencies\n<!--\nPlease provide system dependencies, configuration files\nand other dependency information if applicable\n-->\n<details>\n<p>\nN/A. The reproduction uses kombu's filesystem transport and the file result backend, so the worker's main process and its pool processes share the broker and the results without a server.\n</p>\n</details>\n\n## Minimally Reproducible Test Case\n<!--\nPlease provide a reproducible test case.\nRefer to the Reporting Bugs section in our contribution guide.\n\nWe prefer submitting test cases in the form of a PR to our integration test suite.\nIf you can provide one, please mention the PR number below.\nIf not, please attach the most minimal code example required to reproduce the issue below.\nIf the test case is too large, please include a link to a gist or a repository below.\n\nAlternatively, the pytest-celery plugin can be used to create standalone reproduction scripts\nthat can be added to this report. See the pytest-celery documentation for more information at\npytest-celery.readthedocs.io\n-->\n\n<details>\n<p>\n\nTwo tasks with `ignore_result=True` that are retried once. `retried_once` retries with `Task.retry()`. `lost_once` kills its own pool process, so `task_retry_on_worker_lost` retries it. Both retries run and succeed.\n\n`rtasks.py`:\n\n```python\nimport os\nimport signal\n\nfrom celery import Celery\n\nMARK = os.environ['REPRO_MARK']\n\nROOT = os.path.dirname(MARK)\nfor d in ('q', 'processed', 'results'):\n    os.makedirs(os.path.join(ROOT, d), exist_ok=True)\n\napp = Celery('rtasks', broker='filesystem://',\n             backend='file://' + os.path.join(ROOT, 'results'))\napp.conf.broker_transport_options = {\n    'data_folder_in': os.path.join(ROOT, 'q'),\n    'data_folder_out': os.path.join(ROOT, 'q'),\n    'processed_folder': os.path.join(ROOT, 'processed'),\n}\napp.conf.task_retry_on_worker_lost = True\n\n\n@app.task(bind=True, ignore_result=True, default_retry_delay=0)\ndef lost_once(self):\n    if self.request.retries == 0:\n        os.kill(os.getpid(), signal.SIGKILL)   # the pool process is lost\n    with open(MARK, 'a') as fh:\n        fh.write('lost_once\\n')\n\n\n@app.task(bind=True, ignore_result=True, default_retry_delay=0)\ndef retried_once(self):\n    if self.request.retries == 0:\n        raise self.retry(countdown=0)          # the same retry, via Task.retry()\n    with open(MARK, 'a') as fh:\n        fh.write('retried_once\\n')\n```\n\n`repro.py`, run with `python repro.py` from the same directory:\n\n```python\nimport os\nimport tempfile\nimport time\n\nos.environ.setdefault('REPRO_MARK', os.path.join(tempfile.mkdtemp(), 'ran'))\n\nfrom celery.contrib.testing.worker import start_worker  # noqa: E402\n\nimport rtasks  # noqa: E402\n\n\ndef wait_for(name):\n    for _ in range(600):\n        if os.path.exists(rtasks.MARK) and name in open(rtasks.MARK).read():\n            return True\n        time.sleep(0.1)\n    return False\n\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    with start_worker(rtasks.app, pool='prefork', concurrency=1,\n                      perform_ping_check=False, shutdown_timeout=30):\n        for task in (rtasks.retried_once, rtasks.lost_once):\n            r = task.delay()\n            name = task.name.rsplit('.', 1)[-1]\n            ran = wait_for(name)\n            time.sleep(1)\n            print(f'{name:13} retry ran={ran}  stored state={r.state}')\n```\n\n</p>\n</details>\n\n# Expected Behavior\n<!-- Describe in detail what you expect to happen -->\n\nBoth tasks end the same way. Their results are ignored, so nothing is written to the result backend and both stay `PENDING`, as `retried_once` does:\n\n```\nretried_once  retry ran=True  stored state=PENDING\nlost_once     retry ran=True  stored state=PENDING\n```\n\n# Actual Behavior\n<!--\nDescribe in detail what actually happened.\nPlease include a backtrace and surround it with triple backticks (```).\nIn addition, include the Celery daemon logs, the broker logs,\nthe result backend logs and system logs below if they will help us debug\nthe issue.\n-->\n\nThe retry of `lost_once` runs and succeeds, but its result stays `RETRY` permanently:\n\n```\nretried_once  retry ran=True  stored state=PENDING\nlost_once     retry ran=True  stored state=RETRY\n```\n\n`Request._retry_worker_lost()` in `celery/worker/request.py` calls `task.backend.mark_as_retry()` without checking whether the result is stored. `Task.retry()` goes through `TraceInfo.handle_retry()` in `celery/app/trace.py`, which only calls `mark_as_retry()` when `store_errors` is true. That is false for an ignored result unless `store_errors_even_if_ignored` is set. The retried run of an ignored result stores nothing, so the `RETRY` written by the worker is never replaced.\n\nThe same happens when only the call ignores the result, e.g. `apply_async(ignore_result=True)` on a task that stores results, since the retry now keeps that option (#10958). Every other failure path in `Request` already passes `store_result=self.store_errors`.\n\nI only tried the prefork pool on macOS with Python 3.14, and the filesystem broker and file backend, since the bug doesn't depend on the broker or backend.\n\n", "hints_text": "", "created_at": "2026-11-03T07:41:54Z"}
{"repo": "celery/celery", "pull_number": 10998, "instance_id": "celery__celery-10998", "issue_numbers": ["10997"], "base_commit": "5d83c46ebb3f7183998f55fa2e5af0ad0038b278", "patch": "diff --git a/celery/backends/redis.py b/celery/backends/redis.py\nindex d5011fe75f4..2a6da4618e6 100644\n--- a/celery/backends/redis.py\n+++ b/celery/backends/redis.py\n@@ -1,4 +1,5 @@\n \"\"\"Redis result store backend.\"\"\"\n+import math\n import select\n import selectors\n import threading\n@@ -8,6 +9,7 @@\n from functools import partial\n from ssl import CERT_NONE, CERT_OPTIONAL, CERT_REQUIRED\n from urllib.parse import unquote\n+from uuid import uuid4\n \n from kombu.utils import symbol_by_name\n from kombu.utils.functional import retry_over_time\n@@ -17,6 +19,7 @@\n \n from celery import states\n from celery._state import task_join_will_block\n+from celery.app.amqp import _callback_publish_max_retries\n from celery.backends.base import _create_chord_error_with_cause\n from celery.canvas import maybe_signature\n from celery.exceptions import BackendStoreError, ChordError, ImproperlyConfigured\n@@ -86,10 +89,23 @@\n # redelivered after a lost worker when using acks_late), and must only count\n # once, even if the runs returned different results. Returns the number of\n # results recorded so far, and the chord's total diff and size.\n+#\n+# When the chord completes, this script atomically acquires the callback\n+# dispatch claim within the same execution. This prevents a race where two\n+# workers both detect completion and attempt to dispatch the callback.\n CHORD_PART_RETURN_LUA = \"\"\"\n-local jkey, tkey, skey, dkey, gkey = KEYS[1], KEYS[2], KEYS[3], KEYS[4], KEYS[5]\n+local jkey, tkey, skey, dkey, gkey, ckey = KEYS[1], KEYS[2], KEYS[3], KEYS[4], KEYS[5], KEYS[6]\n local tid, value, ordered, score = ARGV[1], ARGV[2], ARGV[3], ARGV[4]\n local expires, group_expires = tonumber(ARGV[5]), tonumber(ARGV[6])\n+local claim_expires = tonumber(ARGV[7])\n+local claim_token = ARGV[8]\n+\n+-- Prevent late duplicates from recreating chord state after successful cleanup.\n+local done_marker = redis.call('GET', ckey)\n+if done_marker == 'done' then\n+    return {-1, 0, 0, 0}\n+end\n+\n -- Key the check on the task id and header index, so it doesn't merge two\n -- header entries that share the task id of a reused frozen signature.\n local member = tid .. ':' .. score\n@@ -115,7 +131,54 @@\n         redis.call('EXPIRE', gkey, group_expires)\n     end\n end\n-return {readycount, redis.call('GET', tkey), redis.call('GET', skey)}\n+\n+local totaldiff = redis.call('GET', tkey)\n+local size = redis.call('GET', skey)\n+local claimed = 0\n+if size and readycount == tonumber(size) + tonumber(totaldiff or 0) then\n+    if redis.call('SET', ckey, claim_token, 'NX', 'EX', claim_expires) then\n+        claimed = 1\n+    end\n+end\n+\n+return {readycount, totaldiff, size, claimed}\n+\"\"\"\n+\n+# Release the claim and remove chord data atomically if the token matches.\n+# After successful cleanup, set a done marker to prevent late duplicates from\n+# recreating chord state or dispatching the callback again.\n+CHORD_CLEANUP_LUA = \"\"\"\n+local ckey = KEYS[1]\n+local jkey = KEYS[2]\n+local tkey = KEYS[3]\n+local skey = KEYS[4]\n+local dkey = KEYS[5]\n+local token = ARGV[1]\n+local done_expires = tonumber(ARGV[2])\n+\n+if redis.call('GET', ckey) == token then\n+    redis.call('DEL', jkey, tkey, skey, dkey)\n+    if done_expires and done_expires > 0 then\n+        redis.call('SET', ckey, 'done', 'EX', done_expires)\n+    end\n+    return 1\n+end\n+return 0\n+\"\"\"\n+\n+# Extend a dispatch lease while this worker still owns it, or reacquire an\n+# expired lease while chord data remains. The checks and updates are atomic.\n+CHORD_CLAIM_EXTEND_LUA = \"\"\"\n+local ckey, skey = KEYS[1], KEYS[2]\n+local token = ARGV[1]\n+local expires = tonumber(ARGV[2])\n+if redis.call('GET', ckey) == token then\n+    return redis.call('EXPIRE', ckey, expires)\n+end\n+if not redis.call('GET', ckey) and redis.call('EXISTS', skey) == 1 then\n+    return redis.call('SET', ckey, token, 'EX', expires, 'NX') and 1 or 0\n+end\n+return 0\n \"\"\"\n \n logger = get_logger(__name__)\n@@ -797,6 +860,11 @@ def _set_chord_key(self, key, value):\n         return self.ensure(set_key, (key, value))\n \n     def set_chord_size(self, group_id, chord_size):\n+        # Reapplying a frozen chord reuses its group id, but represents a new run.\n+        self.ensure(\n+            self.client.delete,\n+            (self.get_key_for_group(group_id, '.c'),),\n+        )\n         self._set_chord_key(self.get_key_for_group(group_id, '.s'), chord_size)\n \n     def apply_chord(self, header_result_args, body, **kwargs):\n@@ -825,6 +893,44 @@ def _transport_options(self):\n     def _chord_part_return_script(self):\n         return self.client.register_script(CHORD_PART_RETURN_LUA)\n \n+    @cached_property\n+    def _chord_cleanup_script(self):\n+        return self.client.register_script(CHORD_CLEANUP_LUA)\n+\n+    @cached_property\n+    def _chord_claim_extend_script(self):\n+        return self.client.register_script(CHORD_CLAIM_EXTEND_LUA)\n+\n+    def _chord_publish_claim_expires(self, initial_expires, callback):\n+        \"\"\"Estimate the time needed for callback publish retries.\"\"\"\n+        conf = self.app.conf\n+        callback_options = callback.options\n+        default_policy = conf.task_publish_retry_policy or {}\n+        policy = dict(default_policy)\n+        policy.update(callback_options.get('retry_policy') or {})\n+        retry = callback_options.get('retry')\n+        if retry is None:\n+            retry = conf.task_publish_retry\n+        retries = (\n+            _callback_publish_max_retries(policy, default_policy)\n+            if retry else 0\n+        )\n+        timeout = conf.broker_connection_timeout\n+        if timeout is None:\n+            return initial_expires * 2\n+        retries = max(0, int(retries))\n+        timeout = max(0, float(timeout))\n+        start = float(policy.get('interval_start', 0))\n+        step = float(policy.get('interval_step', 0.2))\n+        maximum = float(policy.get('interval_max', 1))\n+        waits = sum(min(start + step * n, maximum) for n in range(retries))\n+        # This is an estimate of connection-attempt time, with one additional\n+        # connection timeout to leave room for publish and broker confirmation.\n+        return max(\n+            initial_expires,\n+            math.ceil((retries + 1) * timeout + waits + max(timeout, 1)),\n+        )\n+\n     def on_chord_part_return(self, request, state, result,\n                              propagate=None, **kwargs):\n         app = self.app\n@@ -839,22 +945,43 @@ def on_chord_part_return(self, request, state, result,\n         tkey = self.get_key_for_group(gid, '.t')\n         skey = self.get_key_for_group(gid, '.s')\n         dkey = self.get_key_for_group(gid, '.d')\n+        ckey = self.get_key_for_group(gid, '.c')\n         result = self.encode_result(result, state)\n         encoded = self.encode([1, tid, state, result])\n-        readycount, totaldiff, chord_size_bytes = self._chord_part_return_script(\n-            keys=[jkey, tkey, skey, dkey, self.get_key_for_group(gid)],\n+\n+        # Keep the initial claim tied to the join timeout for crash recovery.\n+        # The publishing retry budget is added only after joining, just before\n+        # callback.delay(), so slow publishing does not consume that budget.\n+        #\n+        # When result_chord_join_timeout is None, the join can wait indefinitely\n+        # but the claim still has a bounded lifetime (default 10 seconds). This is\n+        # a known trade-off: a worker with an unbounded join timeout could lose\n+        # its claim to another worker while still waiting, potentially causing a\n+        # duplicate dispatch. Users requiring unbounded joins should be aware of\n+        # this limitation.\n+        join_timeout = app.conf.result_chord_join_timeout or 5.0\n+        claim_expires = max(5, int(join_timeout * 2))\n+        claim_token = uuid4().hex\n+\n+        done_expires = int(max(claim_expires * 2, 300))\n+\n+        readycount, totaldiff, chord_size_bytes, claimed = self._chord_part_return_script(\n+            keys=[jkey, tkey, skey, dkey, self.get_key_for_group(gid), ckey],\n             args=[tid, encoded, 1 if self._chord_zset else 0, group_index,\n-                  self.chord_expires or 0, self._chord_result_expires],\n+                  self.chord_expires or 0, self._chord_result_expires,\n+                  claim_expires, claim_token],\n             client=client,\n         )\n \n-        totaldiff = int(totaldiff or 0)\n+        if readycount == -1:\n+            return\n \n         if chord_size_bytes:\n             try:\n                 callback = maybe_signature(request.chord, app=app)\n-                total = int(chord_size_bytes) + totaldiff\n-                if readycount == total:\n+                totaldiff = int(totaldiff or 0)\n+                total = int(chord_size_bytes or 0) + totaldiff\n+                if readycount == total and claimed:\n                     header_result = GroupResult.restore(gid, app=app)\n                     if header_result is not None:\n                         # If we manage to restore a `GroupResult`, then it must\n@@ -888,6 +1015,20 @@ def on_chord_part_return(self, request, state, result,\n                                 pipeline = pipe.lrange(jkey, 0, total)\n                             resl, = pipeline.execute()\n                         resl = [unpack(tup, decode) for tup in resl]\n+                    publish_expires = self._chord_publish_claim_expires(\n+                        claim_expires, callback,\n+                    )\n+                    extended = self._chord_claim_extend_script(\n+                        keys=[ckey, skey],\n+                        args=[claim_token, publish_expires],\n+                        client=client,\n+                    )\n+                    if not extended:\n+                        logger.warning(\n+                            'Chord callback for %r not published: dispatch '\n+                            'claim is no longer owned by this worker', gid,\n+                        )\n+                        return\n                     try:\n                         app.amqp._retry_publish(callback.delay, resl)\n                     except Exception as exc:  # pylint: disable=broad-except\n@@ -898,13 +1039,16 @@ def on_chord_part_return(self, request, state, result,\n                             ChordError(f'Callback error: {exc!r}'),\n                         )\n                     finally:\n-                        with client.pipeline() as pipe:\n-                            pipe \\\n-                                .delete(jkey) \\\n-                                .delete(tkey) \\\n-                                .delete(skey) \\\n-                                .delete(dkey) \\\n-                                .execute()\n+                        cleaned = self._chord_cleanup_script(\n+                            keys=[ckey, jkey, tkey, skey, dkey],\n+                            args=[claim_token, done_expires],\n+                            client=client,\n+                        )\n+                        if not cleaned:\n+                            logger.warning(\n+                                'Chord callback claim for %r was lost before '\n+                                'cleanup; chord data was left for expiry', gid,\n+                            )\n             except ChordError as exc:\n                 logger.exception('Chord %r raised: %r', request.group, exc)\n                 try:\n", "test_patch": "diff --git a/t/integration/test_canvas.py b/t/integration/test_canvas.py\nindex 7165bb88204..a925cb69411 100644\n--- a/t/integration/test_canvas.py\n+++ b/t/integration/test_canvas.py\n@@ -2062,6 +2062,31 @@ def test_chord_order(self, manager):\n         result = c()\n         assert result.get() == inputs\n \n+    def test_reapplying_frozen_chord_dispatches_body_again(self, manager):\n+        \"\"\"A frozen chord reuses its group id, but each apply is a new run.\"\"\"\n+        if not manager.app.conf.result_backend.startswith('redis'):\n+            pytest.skip('Requires redis result backend.')\n+\n+        redis_connection = get_redis_connection()\n+        redis_key = f'frozen-chord-{uuid.uuid4().hex}'\n+        redis_connection.delete(redis_key)\n+        task = chord(\n+            group(add.s(1, 2), add.s(3, 4)),\n+            redis_count.si(redis_key),\n+        )\n+        task.freeze()\n+\n+        try:\n+            first = task.apply_async()\n+            first.get(timeout=TIMEOUT)\n+            await_redis_count(1, redis_key=redis_key)\n+\n+            second = task.apply_async()\n+            second.get(timeout=TIMEOUT)\n+            await_redis_count(2, redis_key=redis_key)\n+        finally:\n+            redis_connection.delete(redis_key)\n+\n     def test_group_or_task_countdown_delays_header(self, manager):\n         \"\"\"countdown on group|task must delay header tasks (#7851).\"\"\"\n         try:\ndiff --git a/t/unit/backends/test_redis.py b/t/unit/backends/test_redis.py\nindex 54a43204d47..d40332abf92 100644\n--- a/t/unit/backends/test_redis.py\n+++ b/t/unit/backends/test_redis.py\n@@ -24,6 +24,7 @@\n from celery import signature, states, uuid\n from celery.app.amqp import _callback_publish_retry\n from celery.backends.base import COMPRESSED_PAYLOAD_MAGIC\n+from celery.backends.redis import CHORD_CLAIM_EXTEND_LUA, CHORD_CLEANUP_LUA, CHORD_PART_RETURN_LUA\n from celery.canvas import Signature\n from celery.contrib.testing.mocks import ContextMock\n from celery.exceptions import BackendStoreError, ChordError, ImproperlyConfigured, WorkerLostError\n@@ -93,10 +94,28 @@ def __init__(self, host=None, port=None, db=None, password=None, **kw):\n         self.db = db\n         self.password = password\n         self.keyspace = {}\n-        self.expiry = {}\n+        self.expiry = {}  # Maps key -> absolute expiration timestamp\n+        self.current_time = 0  # Controllable clock for TTL simulation\n         self.connection = self.Connection()\n \n+    def advance_time(self, seconds):\n+        \"\"\"Advance the mock clock by the specified number of seconds.\"\"\"\n+        self.current_time += seconds\n+        # Clean up expired keys\n+        expired_keys = [\n+            key for key, expiry in self.expiry.items()\n+            if expiry <= self.current_time\n+        ]\n+        for key in expired_keys:\n+            self.keyspace.pop(key, None)\n+            self.expiry.pop(key, None)\n+\n     def get(self, key):\n+        # Check if key has expired\n+        if key in self.expiry and self.expiry[key] <= self.current_time:\n+            self.keyspace.pop(key, None)\n+            self.expiry.pop(key, None)\n+            return None\n         return self.keyspace.get(key)\n \n     def mget(self, keys):\n@@ -106,13 +125,17 @@ def setex(self, key, expires, value):\n         self.set(key, value)\n         self.expire(key, expires)\n \n-    def set(self, key, value, ex=None):\n+    def set(self, key, value, ex=None, nx=False):\n+        if nx and key in self.keyspace:\n+            return None  # Key already exists, NX fails\n         self.keyspace[key] = value\n         if ex:\n             self.expire(key, ex)\n+        return True\n \n     def expire(self, key, expires):\n-        self.expiry[key] = expires\n+        # Store absolute expiration timestamp (current_time + expires)\n+        self.expiry[key] = self.current_time + expires\n         return expires\n \n     def delete(self, key):\n@@ -171,29 +194,78 @@ def sadd(self, key, value):\n         return 1\n \n     def register_script(self, script):\n-        # Only the chord part script of the backend is used; emulate it\n-        # with the fake commands above.\n-        def chord_part_return(keys, args, client=None):\n-            jkey, tkey, skey, dkey, gkey = keys\n-            tid, value, ordered, score, expires, group_expires = args\n-            member = f'{tid}:{score}'\n-            if member not in self.keyspace.get(dkey, set()):\n+        if script == CHORD_CLEANUP_LUA:\n+            def chord_cleanup(keys, args, client=None):\n+                ckey, jkey, tkey, skey, dkey = keys\n+                token = args[0]\n+                done_expires = int(args[1]) if len(args) > 1 else None\n+                current = self.get(ckey)\n+                if current == token.encode() if isinstance(token, str) else token:\n+                    self.delete(jkey)\n+                    self.delete(tkey)\n+                    self.delete(skey)\n+                    self.delete(dkey)\n+                    if done_expires and done_expires > 0:\n+                        self.set(ckey, b'done', ex=done_expires)\n+                    return 1\n+                else:\n+                    return 0\n+            return chord_cleanup\n+        if script == CHORD_CLAIM_EXTEND_LUA:\n+            def chord_claim_extend(keys, args, client=None):\n+                ckey, skey = keys\n+                token, expires = args\n+                current = self.get(ckey)\n+                token = token.encode() if isinstance(token, str) else token\n+                if current == token:\n+                    return int(bool(self.expire(ckey, int(expires))))\n+                if current is None and self.exists(skey):\n+                    return int(bool(self.set(\n+                        ckey, token, ex=int(expires), nx=True,\n+                    )))\n+                return 0\n+            return chord_claim_extend\n+        if script == CHORD_PART_RETURN_LUA:\n+            def chord_part_return(keys, args, client=None):\n+                jkey, tkey, skey, dkey, gkey, ckey = keys\n+                tid, value, ordered, score, expires, group_expires, claim_expire